   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. Four points were estimated rather than read exactly:\n\n- **Acyl chain length:** I estimated it from the drawn length as palmitoyl (C16), \u03b3Glu-linked. A C18 chain is the main alternative.\n- **PEG count:** I counted 12 ether oxygens, 5 in the lower run and 7 on the right side.\n- **Amino-acid stereocentres:** The Pen, Lys, \u03b1-Me-Lys and Glu stereocentres are L-type; I checked the Pen and \u03b1-Me-Lys wedges against the drawing. I assumed L for the Asn, Thr, Trp, Tyr(OMe), Nal, Pal and Glu centres without checking their wedges and hashes.\n- **Thr \u03b2-carbon:** I took the Thr \u03b2-carbon as the L-Thr (3R) configuration.\n\n**Peptide core:**\n- The N-terminus is Ac-Pen, linked through a disulfide to a second Pen, which closes the macrocycle.\n- The ring runs Pen\u2013Asn\u2013Thr\u20137-Me-Trp\u2013Lys(Ac)\u2013Pen.\n- The tail after the ring is Tyr(OMe)\u20132-Nal\u2013\u03b1-Me-Lys\u2013Lys(Ac)\u2013Asn\u20133-Pal\u2013Sar-NH2.\n\n**Lipidated side chain:**\n- The \u03b1-Me-Lys \u03b5-amine carries C(=O)CH2CH2 followed by twelve repeats of O\u2013CH2CH2.\n- This continues to NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2 on the \u03b3-carboxyl of Glu.\n- The Glu \u03b1-amine is acylated by the palmitoyl chain, and its \u03b1-carboxyl is a free acid.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)S%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2c(C)cccc12)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)S%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(OC)cc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)C(=O)N[C@@](C)(CCCCNC(=O)CCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1cccnc1)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O"
